# ============================================================
# Root .gitignore — repo had NONE until 2026-07-30. Every .env
# and .venv across this monorepo was untracked-but-not-ignored,
# one `git add -A` away from landing in this PUBLIC GitHub repo.
# ============================================================

# Secrets — any .env anywhere in the tree, all variants
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env*.example

# Python virtualenvs — any depth, any name
.venv/
venv/
*/.venv/
*/venv/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/

# Node
node_modules/
.next/
out/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# macOS
.DS_Store
._*

# Logs / runtime artifacts
*.log
logs/
call_log.jsonl
outputs/

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Compiled macOS launcher app bundles (built by USS-TJR-Control/platypus-start.sh
# via Platypus) — build output, not source. 4 near-duplicate copies were
# accidentally committed to main in a whole-directory-import merge; removed
# 2026-08-11, ignored here so it doesn't recur.
*.app/

# id_registry.py's fcntl lock file — ephemeral, recreated on every mint.
# Track .id-counters.json itself (it's the durable counter state); never this.
.id-counters.lock

# core/platform/memory_graph.py's embedded FalkorDB Lite store (via
# redislite) — a local binary graph database file, not a durable evidence
# artifact like data/self-improvement/runs/ (which IS tracked) — rebuilt
# from core_events by re-running the backfill, never hand-authored.
data/memory_graph.db*

# 2026-09-05: caught a leak — .infisical-auth.env didn't match .env/.env.*
.infisical-auth.env
*-auth.env

# Chatterbox TTS (core/voice/tts_chatterbox.py, real tracked source) — its
# venv (torch/transformers, multi-GB) and generated-audio disk cache don't
# match the venv/ patterns above (different literal name) and were found
# untracked-but-not-ignored on the VM, same shape of gap that caused the
# .infisical-auth.env leak. Ignored explicitly before that repeats.
core/voice/chatterbox-venv/
core/voice/cache/

# data/self-improvement/review/: the self-improvement engine's live review
# state — mutated continuously between cycles as findings get reviewed
# (decisions.jsonl, opportunities.jsonl) or a cycle runs (.evolution_cycle.lock).
# Unlike data/self-improvement/runs/ (durable per-cycle evidence, tracked
# on purpose), these change outside of any deliberate commit, which kept
# dirtying the VM's working tree and blocking deploy/auto-deploy.sh's
# fast-forward-only pull (confirmed 2026-09-09: divergence + repeated
# "working tree is dirty" aborts). Untracked here; the periodic cycle-summary
# files in the same directory (cycle_summary.json, decision_report.json,
# evolution_summary.json, opportunity_id_counter.txt, remediation_results.jsonl,
# mission_dispatch_log.jsonl, finding_staleness.jsonl) are intentionally
# still committed as each cycle's record and are unaffected by this.
data/self-improvement/review/.evolution_cycle.lock
data/self-improvement/review/decisions.jsonl
data/self-improvement/review/opportunities.jsonl

# cortex_suite (github.com/Artistsyn/cortex_suite) local install, wired into
# core/engineering/context_enricher.py's STRUCTURAL API CONTEXT section.
# .cortex/index-sources.json IS committed (the source-root config); everything
# else here is machine-local, regenerated by `.cortex/cortex.sh reindex`.
.cortex/memory.db
.cortex/apigraph/
.cortex/suite.env
.cortex/cortex.sh
.cortex/cortex.ps1
.cortex/prefs.toml
.mcp.json
CLAUDE.md
.github/copilot-instructions.md

# Local git worktrees created by parallel Claude Code subagents — ephemeral
# per-session checkouts, not repo content.
.claude/worktrees/
